    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAs">III As</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q">Quartum: ne aliquis recipiat alterius hominem sine licencia eius (ipsius) cui ante (prius) folgauit nec intra mercam nec extra;</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#attenborough" n="4" corresp="#wit-q">Quartum, ne aliquis recipiat alterius hominem sine licentia eius cui ante folgavit nec intra mercam nec extra;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-q">Fourthly, no one receive a man who has been in the service of another, without the permission of him he has been serving, whether within our borders or beyond them.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="170">II As [?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IVAs_4">IV As 4</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. Liebermann compares II As 22.</note>
      </div>
